---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const posts = await getCollection("blog");
posts.sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
const latestPosts = posts.slice(0, 5);

// Edit this list to change the timeline. Newest first.
const years = [
  {
    year: "2027",
    text: "The plan is to launch a bunch of apps and write about each one as I build it, so anyone can follow along, including the parts that don't work.",
  },
  {
    year: "2026",
    text: "I had been thinking about starting something of my own for a while, and this year I did. I started ACE Labs, a small product building firm. I met a lot of other builders, started building, and started writing up my research. These days I'm focused on indie hacking.",
  },
  {
    year: "2025",
    text: "I kept at it as a full-stack developer, picked up Python and AI agents with voice, and spent more time in builder and open source communities.",
  },
  {
    year: "2024",
    text: "I got my first internship and it turned into a full-time job. Since then I've worked as a full-stack developer on SaaS and enterprise applications.",
  },
  {
    year: "2023",
    text: "I spent the year in pop-up Discord servers. I was into buildspace but couldn't build anything yet. I was learning and trying to understand the ecosystem.",
  },
];
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>hi, I'm Prasad.</h1>
    <p class="big">I build stuff.</p>
    <p>
      I'm an engineer, a curious problem solver and a continuous learner. I like databases, distributed systems and AI agents. I also like to travel, and I write when the mood strikes.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>my story</h2>
    <p>
      I grew up in a small village where technology was not part of everyday life. I got curious about computers through movies and games, and then more curious about how they worked underneath. It took a while to turn that into a career.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since then I've tried to be the kind of person who does the work in front of me properly, keeps learning in the open, and keeps building on the side. I like understanding how things work one level down, and I like shipping things people can use.
    </p>
    <p>
      The longer version is <a href="/origin-story">here</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>right now</h2>
    <p>
      I haven't built anything yet that I'd call finished, but I'm building right now. I'm making small apps on my own time, going deep on databases, and writing down what I learn as I go, including what doesn't work. Some of that happens through <a href="https://acelabs-hq.github.io/acelabs/">ACE Labs</a>, which I run independently of my day job.
    </p>
    <p>
      My latest deep dive is on <a href="/blog/postgres-notify-global-lock/">the lock hiding behind Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>the last few years</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      {years.map((y) => (
        <li>
          <span class="year">{y.year}</span>
          <p>{y.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>blog</h2>
    <ul class="posts">
      {latestPosts.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <span class="post-date">{post.data.date.toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</span>
          <a href={`/blog/${post.id.replace(".md", "")}/`}>{post.data.title}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/blogs">all posts</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>collection</h2>
    <p>
      Things I keep around:
      <a href="/quotes">quotes</a>,
      <a href="/bucket">bucket list</a>,
      <a href="/research">research</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>say hi</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://x.com/rev_proxy">twitter</a>
      ·
      <a href="mailto:pfirame18@gmail.com">email</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
.hero {
  margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
}

.hero h1 {
  font-size: 2.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
}

.big {
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 500;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

section {
  margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
}

section h2 {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-transform: lowercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
}

.timeline,
.posts {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
}

.timeline li {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 4rem 1fr;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}

.timeline .year {
  font-weight: 600;
}

.timeline p {
  margin: 0;
}

.posts li {
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.9rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
}

.posts .post-date {
  flex: 0 0 5.8rem;
}

@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .timeline li {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0;
  }
  .posts li {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }
}
</style>
